&lt;p&gt;Upwork&#39;s Match Platform team sits at the heart of how clients and freelancers find each other. As Senior Product Manager for Match Platform, you will own the shared infrastructure that powers matching, personalization, embeddings, and evaluation across multiple product surfaces. This is a high-leverage role: the models, features, and frameworks you build become the foundation that other product and ML teams build on. You will partner closely with engineering, data science, machine learning, analytics, and marketplace operations to reduce duplication, increase reuse of shared capabilities, and drive measurable improvements in match quality, and relevance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovate:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive the roadmap for next-generation AI-powered search, recommendation, and matching systems — including retrieval, ranking, personalization infrastructure, and the shared model and feature foundations that multiple product surfaces build on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategize:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the AI/ML product strategy and roadmap, making deliberate tradeoffs between long-term platform investments and near-term surface-specific wins so teams build on a common foundation rather than duplicating work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Apply cutting-edge AI&lt;/strong&gt; to solve high-impact customer problems, including but not limited to:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NLP and intent understanding to better interpret what users are looking for&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embedding-based and neural retrieval for deeper contextual matching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personalized ranking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real-time indexing for fresher, more relevant results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own core models and evaluation systems:&lt;/strong&gt; Set strategy for human labeling programs, offline evaluation frameworks, and online experimentation, and establish a unified data strategy for shared labels, features, and outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead cross-functional alignment across product, engineering, ML, data science, analytics, design, and operations, moving work forward through clarity and trust rather than authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measure success:&lt;/strong&gt; Define instrumentation, key metrics, and operating cadences that connect system-level insights to measurable product improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay on the cutting edge:&lt;/strong&gt; Track emerging AI techniques and tools and bring them into your work early, keeping our search and recommendation capabilities ahead of the curve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What it takes to catch our eye&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience as a product manager working directly on search, recommendation, ranking, or large-scale information retrieval systems, ideally in a marketplace or other two-sided context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep AI/ML fluency — able to partner effectively with engineering and data teams on retrieval methods, ranking signals, embeddings, model tuning, and evaluation, and to translate those concepts into clear product decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of owning platform- or infrastructure-level product work, where your roadmap shaped capabilities other teams depended on, not just user-facing features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success leading experimentation and A/B testing programs and using results to inform roadmap and design decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate ambiguous user and business needs into concrete, technically feasible requirements, and to make sound prioritization calls across systems, teams, and time horizons.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, inclusive communicator who drives cross-functional alignment in fast-paced, technically complex environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
